.SH OPTIONS
GASH is based on GNU Bash, so its command syntax and options are
generally inherited from Bash. Some output and error-message behavior
may differ because of GASH customizations.
.PP
Here are some common options:
.TP
.BI \-c " command_string"
Execute commands from
.IR command_string ,
then exit.
.IP
.B BroTip:
Wrap a command string in quotes when it contains spaces or shell
metacharacters, for example:
.B "gash -c 'git remote -v'"
.TP
.BI \-n " file"
Read commands and check their syntax without executing them.
.IP
.B Warning:
This checks shell syntax, not whether your script's logic is correct
or whether it will behave as you expect.
.IP
.B BroTip:
Want to catch more potential script problems?
Give
.BR shellcheck (1)
a try. It's free. =D
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-login
Make GASH act as if it had been invoked as a login shell.
.PP
For the complete list of options, see
.BR bash (1)
or the Bash reference documentation.
